WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.460
With half a dozen commands you step out

2
00:00:01.460 --> 00:00:02.960
of the chat and put an agent to

3
00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:04.640
work inside your folders.

4
00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:05.800
This is sequence one,

5
00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:08.280
OSWork, and it separates people who use

6
00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:10.320
artificial intelligence from people who create with it.

7
00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:12.300
In this video: why the chat gets stuck,

8
00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:13.600
the terminal steps,

9
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:14.300
and at the end,

10
00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:16.040
the first request for your agent.

11
00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:18.640
In the chat, artificial intelligence can't see

12
00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:19.700
your files,

13
00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:21.260
forgets what you explained yesterday,

14
00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:23.780
and every answer has to be copied and

15
00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:24.320
pasted.

16
00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:26.320
You become the mail carrier between the window

17
00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:26.940
and your work.

18
00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:29.600
OSWork shows the path in three

19
00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:30.840
windows: the Chat,

20
00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:32.420
the Work and the Desktop.

21
00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:33.340
And then the terminal,

22
00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:34.480
where the agent lives.

23
00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:35.640
The terminal looks scary,

24
00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:36.840
but it's just another window.

25
00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:38.980
You type a command and it answers.

26
00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:40.720
With six commands you navigate:

27
00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:41.620
see where you are,

28
00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:43.360
list, enter a folder,

29
00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:44.940
go back, create a folder,

30
00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:45.900
open a file.

31
00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:46.780
It's not programming.

32
00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:48.520
It's walking through your folders without the

33
00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:48.860
mouse.

34
00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:50.560
The secret is in the folders.

35
00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:51.660
One folder per project,

36
00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:53.680
and inside it, text files in

37
00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:54.180
markdown.

38
00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:56.080
One of them is AGENTS dot MD:

39
00:00:56.080 --> 00:00:57.420
the project's rules,

40
00:00:57.420 --> 00:00:58.100
who you are,

41
00:00:58.100 --> 00:00:59.140
what it can and what it

42
00:00:59.140 --> 00:00:59.560
can't do.

43
00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:01.340
The agent reads this file every time

44
00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:01.900
it starts.

45
00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:03.280
It's like handing the manual to a

46
00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:04.080
new employee.

47
00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:05.060
Now the agent.

48
00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:06.800
You go into the project folder and

49
00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:08.880
call Claude Code or Codex.

50
00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:11.040
Ask: create a simple page about me

51
00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:12.700
and a file with the rules for this

52
00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:13.360
project.

53
00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:14.920
The files appear in the folder.

54
00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:16.160
You didn't program anything.

55
00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:16.960
You gave the task,

56
00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:18.740
checked the result and decided.

57
00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:19.960
That's management.

58
00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:21.280
Then comes security.

59
00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:23.020
Git saves every version,

60
00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:24.240
and if the agent makes a mistake,

61
00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:24.860
you go back.

62
00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:27.160
Keys and passwords stay out of the

63
00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:28.960
text, in a secrets file.

64
00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:30.380
And at the end of the path,

65
00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:32.220
Telegram becomes the interface,

66
00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:34.860
and a VPS keeps the agent running

67
00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:36.540
even with your computer turned off.

68
00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:38.080
This is the step that unlocks the

69
00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:39.180
other three sequences:

70
00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:41.300
Jarvis, the queues and the networks

71
00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:42.260
on autopilot.

72
00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:43.460
The complete OSWork,

73
00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:44.420
command by command,

74
00:01:44.420 --> 00:01:45.960
is on INEMA dot CLUB,

75
00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:47.260
open and free.

76
00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:48.520
Open the terminal today,

77
00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:49.620
create your first folder,

78
00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:51.000
and give your agent its first task

79
00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:51.740
.
